  "summary": "A short profile of Dr Ronja Oyelaran, Senior Lecturer in the School of Emergent Priorities, told largely in her own words. A former adviser to a state planning authority, Dr Oyelaran traces what becomes of the views a consultation invites, from a bus-stop comment box that counts every slip as a completed consultation to a smoke-alarm survey in which the word \"working\" meant six different things. The video also marks her research funding, among the ten highest at the University, from the Anticipatory Capability Fund.",
